    "text": "Aaand, the results are in:\n\nBest Solo Game\n#1: Packs Kingdoms by B. Hazard\n#2: Base of Spades by Gregg Jewell\n#3: Cardbury by Iffix Y Santaph\n#4: Black◆Diamond by D. Teuber\n#5: Alice's Nightmares by Vittorio Musella\n#6: Jack's Nightmare by Clark Anderson\n#7: Chapel by quantum potato\n#8: River Rats by M. & Robin Stokkel\n#9: Troll Forest by Mike L\n#10: Abroad by Edin Mujadžević\n\nBest Multiplayer Game\n#1: Packs Kingdoms by B. Hazard\n#2: Puzzle Poker by Vincent Bugica\n#3: Chowdah by John Burton\n#4: Starships by ForgetMeTomorrow\n#5: RoboRummy by Clark Anderson\n#6: Roofs by Jacob Buss\n#7: QUINT by J Simmons\n#8: You see what I must dream by Leo Cidner\n#9: Quarters by Ákos Plesznivy & Petra Hahn\n#10: River Rats by M. & Robin Stokkel\n\nBest Rulebook\n#1: Gregg Jewell for Base of Spades\n#2: Clark Anderson for Jack's Nightmare\n#3: John Burton for Chowdah\n#4: Iffix Y Santaph for Cardbury\n#5: Robin Stokkel for River Rats\n#6: B. Hazard for Packs Kingdoms\n#7: Jacob Zimmerman for Commitment\n#8: D. Teuber for Black◆Diamond\n#9: quantum potato for Chapel\n#10: Clark Anderson for RoboRummy\n\nBest Use of Theme\n#1: Chapel by quantum potato\n#2: RoboRummy by Clark Anderson\n#3: Packs Kingdoms by B. Hazard\n#4: Sinbad and the Seven Isles by Constance Metzinger\n#5: Starships by ForgetMeTomorrow\n#6: Troll Forest by Mike L\n#7: Measure and Tempo by Jacob Zimmerman\n#8: River Rats by M. & Robin Stokkel\n#9: Checkmate in Your Pocket by Kendall Woffinden\n#10: Abroad by Edin Mujadžević\n\nMost Innovative Mechanic\n#1: Chapel by quantum potato\n#2: Abroad by Edin Mujadžević\n#3: Cardbury by Iffix Y Santaph\n#4: Checkmate in Your Pocket by Kendall Woffinden\n#5: Jack's Nightmare by Clark Anderson\n#6: Base of Spades by Gregg Jewell\n#7: RoboRummy by Clark Anderson\n#8: Packs Kingdoms by B. Hazard\n#9: Black◆Diamond by D. Teuber\n#10: Starships by ForgetMeTomorrow\n\nBest Game with Theme \"Dream World\"\n#1: Troll Forest by Mike L\n#2: Alice's Nightmares by Vittorio Musella\n#3: You see what I must dream by Leo Cidner\n#4: Jack's Nightmare by Clark Anderson\n#5: Night Dungeon by Qu1rr3l\n\nMost Valuable Playtester\n\n#2: BrianK24\n#3: Platonic Fool\n#4: Uberdante\n#5: Frank\n\nMany thanks to the fantastic Ben Morayta for taking care of the voting part of the contest!\n\nCongratulations to the winners, runner ups and everyone who has created and entered a game! Many thanks to all the playtesters as well!\n\nIt's been a great contest with many awesome entries this year! See you all again next time, and I wish you all the best in the New Year!",
    "tokens": "\nAaand, the results are in:\n\nBest Solo Game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#1: Packs Kingdoms by \nB. Hazard\n#2: Base of Spades by \nGregg Jewell\n#3: Cardbury by \nIffix Y Santaph\n#4: Black◆Diamond by \nD. Teuber\n#5: Alice's Nightmares by \nVittorio Musella\n#6: Jack's Nightmare by \nClark Anderson\n#7: Chapel by \nquantum potato\n#8: River Rats by M. & \nRobin Stokkel\n#9: Troll Forest by \nMike L\n#10: Abroad by \nEdin Mujadžević\n\nBest Multiplayer Game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#1: Packs Kingdoms by \nB. Hazard\n#2: Puzzle Poker by \nVincent Bugica\n#3: Chowdah by \nJohn Burton\n#4: Starships by \nForgetMeTomorrow\n#5: RoboRummy by \nClark Anderson\n#6: Roofs by \nJacob Buss\n#7: QUINT by \nJ Simmons\n#8: You see what I must dream by \nLeo Cidner\n#9: Quarters by \nÁkos Plesznivy & Petra Hahn\n#10: River Rats by M. & \nRobin Stokkel\n\nBest Rulebook\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#1: \nGregg Jewell for Base of Spades\n#2: \nClark Anderson for Jack's Nightmare\n#3: \nJohn Burton for Chowdah\n#4: \nIffix Y Santaph for Cardbury\n#5: \nRobin Stokkel for River Rats\n#6: \nB. Hazard for Packs Kingdoms\n#7: \nJacob Zimmerman for Commitment\n#8: \nD. Teuber for Black◆Diamond\n#9: \nquantum potato for Chapel\n#10: \nClark Anderson for RoboRummy\n\nBest Use of Theme\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#1: Chapel by \nquantum potato\n#2: RoboRummy by \nClark Anderson\n#3: Packs Kingdoms by \nB. Hazard\n#4: Sinbad and the Seven Isles by \nConstance Metzinger\n#5: Starships by \nForgetMeTomorrow\n#6: Troll Forest by \nMike L\n#7: Measure and Tempo by \nJacob Zimmerman\n#8: River Rats by M. & \nRobin Stokkel\n#9: Checkmate in Your Pocket by \nKendall Woffinden\n#10: Abroad by \nEdin Mujadžević\n\nMost Innovative Mechanic\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#1: Chapel by \nquantum potato\n#2: Abroad by \nEdin Mujadžević\n#3: Cardbury by \nIffix Y Santaph\n#4: Checkmate in Your Pocket by \nKendall Woffinden\n#5: Jack's Nightmare by \nClark Anderson\n#6: Base of Spades by \nGregg Jewell\n#7: RoboRummy by \nClark Anderson\n#8: Packs Kingdoms by \nB. Hazard\n#9: Black◆Diamond by \nD. Teuber\n#10: Starships by \nForgetMeTomorrow\n\nBest Game with Theme \"Dream World\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#1: Troll Forest by \nMike L\n#2: Alice's Nightmares by \nVittorio Musella\n#3: You see what I must dream by \nLeo Cidner\n#4: Jack's Nightmare by \nClark Anderson\n#5: Night Dungeon by  \nQu1rr3l\n\nMost Valuable Playtester\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#1: \nKaren Robinson\n#2: \nBrianK24\n#3: \nPlatonic Fool\n#4: \nUberdante\n#5: \nFrank\n\nMany thanks to the fantastic Ben Morayta for taking care of the voting part of the contest!\n\nCongratulations to the winners, runner ups and everyone who has created and entered a game! Many thanks to all the playtesters as well! \n\nIt's been a great contest with many awesome entries this year! See you all again next time, and I wish you all the best in the New Year!",
